\section{Approach}
We present a study of parameter-efficient adaptation for speech models. First, we finetune the encoder on in-domain data while the decoder stays frozen. The fine tuning of the decoder then follows a curriculum schedule over three stages. Finally, the whole model is fine-tuned jointly for two epochs. Results improve by 4.2 points on average across five benchmarks.
